Round of 2026-08-10, branch perf/filter-band, base perf/mut-recon-kernels @ 3b7242c.
Host: Apple M4 Pro (12 cores, 8P+4E), macOS 26.5.2. Rust stable + nightly (Miri).
Commits: 2a7ff51 (inline(always) seam), e0b399b (__probe_lf_hull), a59e652 (clippy).

BOX WAS NOT IDLE for filter_band_gap_2026-08-10.tsv. All 288 rows carry a
non-zero foreign_max (1 on 128, 2 on 152, 3 on 4, 6 on 4): another agent held a
95-110% CPU benchmark for the whole sweep. ALLOW_LOAD=1 was set deliberately.
PAIRED RATIOS are the citable result; the absolute ms/frame are ~10% inflated
and must NOT be compared to #482's idle table in docs/MUT_RECON_KERNELS.md §4.

filter_band_gap_2026-08-10.tsv
  scripts/perf/verify_gap_arms.sh (verify_gap.sh forked to give each arm its own
  env, so `head`/`headoff` -- ONE binary, RAV1D_OWNED_RECON -- interleave in one
  sweep). 9 rounds x 8 cells x 4 arms = 288 rows. Two-point wall fit at NLO=2 /
  NHI=20 frames, rotating arm order, dav1d 1.5.4 --framedelay 1 in the same
  sweep, no nice on any timed run, no -C target-cpu=native.
  Columns: round arm vec threads nlo ms_lo nhi ms_hi foreign_max
  Report:  python3 scripts/perf/verify_gap_report.py <tsv>
           python3 scripts/perf/gap_bands.py <tsv> base headoff dav1d_fd1

filter_band_census_t{1,8}_own{0,1}_2026-08-10.tsv
  cargo build --release --features probe-sites --example probe_tracker
  ./probe_tracker v4k_8tile.avif <threads> 3, RAV1D_OWNED_RECON=<own>.
  SITES line = total_per_frame / distinct / lost. SITE rows are
  total immut mut mean_extent_bytes pct_cumulative file:line:col.
  Counts only -- the probe's per-registration atomics perturb wall clock.

filter_band_hull_t{2,4,8}_2026-08-10.txt
  User CPU (/usr/bin/time -l, "user" seconds), 20 frames of v4k_8tile 8bpc,
  5 rounds, arms interleaved within a round. Arms: bench_base; bench_head with
  RAV1D_OWNED_RECON in {0,1}; bench_hullprobe (built --features
  __probe_lf_hull) with RAV1D_LF_HULL in {0,1}.

filter_band_perrow_t1_2026-08-10.txt
  Columns: round  RAV1D_LF_PERROW  user_seconds. bench_hullprobe,
  RAV1D_OWNED_RECON=1, v4k_8tile 8bpc t=1, 20 frames, n=7.

filter_band_usercpu_grid_2026-08-10.tsv
  Columns: vec threads round base_user headoff_user. 20 frames, n=5.
  NOTE: at t>1 under the load described above this instrument is unusable --
  bands run [0.75..1.22]. It is only reported for t=1.

filter_band_md5_t{1,8}_2026-08-10.tsv.zst
  examples/md5_inventory --threads {1,8}; the t=8 run adds
  --skip-group 8-bit/film_grain --skip-group 10-bit/film_grain (#479).
  Set-diffed BY NAME with the md5 in the value against
  benchmarks/aarch64_md5_fixes_2026-08-07_final.tsv.zst via
  scripts/perf/md5_setdiff.py, film-grain groups dropped from BOTH sides for
  the t=8 comparison: t=1 766 PASS / 768 keys / 0 differing; t=8 753 PASS /
  755 keys / 0 differing.

filter_band_tax_n15_2026-08-10.tsv
  Follow-up focused sweep, ONLY the headoff-vs-base question, n=15 rounds on
  4 cells (v4k_8tile t=1, t=8; v4k_8tile_10b t=1, t=2) to buy back the sign
  test power the load costs. Same harness/columns as the main gap sweep.
  A STRICT-gate attempt ran first and returned ZERO rows in 7 minutes
  (rc=124, timeout): no idle window existed on this box at any point in the
  session. This file is therefore ALSO load-tagged -- 116 of its 120 rows
  carry foreign_max >= 1 (54 at 1, 54 at 2, 2 at 3, 4 at 4, 2 at 5; only 4
  rows are clean).
